@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Maintainer image pipeline — proveo build / test / deploy

actor "Maintainer" as MT

node "Maintainer host" as HOST <<host>> {
  component "mise tasks\nbuild · test-defs · deploy" as MISE <<app>>
  component "cmd/proveo build|test|deploy\n(internal/maintain)" as CMD <<app>>
  component "internal/manifest\nharness.manifest set" as MAN <<app>>
  component "Registry(ms, defsDir) → []Target\nname · kind · image · defDir\nbuildScript · buildArgs · testScript" as REG <<app>>
  component "defs/<name>/build.sh\n→ defs/lib/docker-build.sh (buildx)" as BUILD <<app>>
  component "defs/<name>/test.sh\nimage contract suites" as TEST <<app>>
}

folder "Target kinds" as KINDS <<host>> {
  component "base\nbase · base-node · base-node-lsp\nbase-node-browser" as KB <<app>>
  component "harness\nfrom images{} — incl. variants\n(claudecode-solidity, -browser)" as KH <<app>>
  component "sidecar\nsquid-proxy · egress-proxy\nmitmproxy · dind" as KS <<app>>
}

cloud "Registry (docker push)" as REGISTRY <<cloud>>

MT ARROW_MAIN MISE
MISE ARROW_MAIN CMD : " ""go run ./cmd/proveo build …"" "
CMD ARROW_MAIN MAN : enumerate defs
MAN ARROW_MAIN REG
REG ARROW_MAIN KINDS : one Target per buildable image
REG ARROW_MAIN BUILD : local → buildx ""--load"" (host arch)
REG ARROW_OPTIONAL TEST : ""proveo test <target>""
BUILD ARROW_CLOUD REGISTRY : deploy → buildx ""--push""\n""PROVEO_PLATFORMS"" (default linux/amd64,linux/arm64)

note right of REG
  **Derived, never hardcoded.** The buildable set comes
  from the manifest ""images"" map plus a fixed sidecar
  list (sidecars have no harness manifest). A variant is
  a Target whose ""buildArgs"" carry the selector, e.g.
  ""--variant mcp"" — so ""claudecode"" and
  ""claudecode-solidity"" share one def dir and one build.sh.
end note

note bottom of BUILD
  Local builds ""--load"" the host platform only, because
  a multi-arch manifest list cannot be loaded into the
  local docker image store. Multi-arch exists only on
  the ""--push"" path.

  Bases are ensured before dependents: a harness build
  invokes its base's ""ensure.sh"" first, so
  ""base-node-lsp"" exists before claudecode/opencode
  build ""FROM"" it.
end note

note bottom of TEST
  Image contract suites assert the *runtime* contract —
  non-root default user, baked tooling, seeded defaults,
  entrypoint bridging — against the built image, not the
  source. Grep-the-source assertions are retired
  (see _spec/tests/20-contract.puml).
end note
note bottom of REG
  **Registry order is build order, and it is hand-made rather than sorted.**
  The base image first, then harness targets by name, then the egress
  sidecars — so a caller iterating the registry never builds a child before
  its parent.

  **Build and deploy answer different questions, so they are different
  plans.** ""BuildPlan"" leaves the image tagged locally through
  ""defs/lib/docker-build\.sh"", which ""--load""s a single platform; ""DeployPlan""
  rebuilds with ""buildx --push"" for ""linux/amd64,linux/arm64"". A plain
  ""docker push"" of a locally built image cannot substitute — it would
  publish one architecture under a manifest the fleet expects to be
  multi-arch. The verify step's ""docker image inspect"" is run quiet because
  its //failure// is the signal, not its output.
end note

note bottom of CMD
  **Target selection has three shapes and one ordering rule.** An explicit
  name, the literal ""all"", or — with no argument on a TTY — a picker:
  type-to-filter, ""Tab"" toggles several (space is reserved for the filter
  query, which is why Tab is the multi-select key), ""Enter"" confirms.

  The chosen set is then returned **in registry order, not in
  Tab-selection order**, because build order matters and the operator's
  click sequence carries no dependency information.
end note


@enduml
